                     sold, rented or monetized; or using it to obtain grants, prizes or contracts
                     for anyone other than the team.

2. What you MAY do (free of charge)
   a. Read and study the Software, and cite it.
   b. Download it and run it on your own devices for personal, educational, research, journalistic
      or evaluation purposes that are not Commercial use.
   c. Make changes in a fork hosted on the same platform as the Official repository, ONLY to prepare
      and submit Contributions back to the Official repository.
   d. Share links to the Official repository and quote short excerpts with attribution.

3. What you may NOT do
   a. Any Commercial use of the Software or of any work based on it.
